msgid "contentType.format(obj)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/content-type_README.md:71
msgid ""
"Format an object into a `Content-Type` header. This will return a string "
"of the content type for the given object with the following properties "
"(examples are shown that produce the string `'image/svg+xml; "
"charset=utf-8'`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/content-type_README.md:75
msgid "`type`: The media type (will be lower-cased). Example: `'image/svg+xml'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/content-type_README.md:77
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`parameters`: An object of the parameters in the media type (name of the "
"parameter will be lower-cased). Example: `{charset: 'utf-8'}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/content-type_README.md:80
msgid ""
"Throws a `TypeError` if the object contains an invalid type or parameter "
"names."
